/* book Worked example: Q: A Class AB PA runs from VDD = 3.3 V with an average current of 300 mA. It delivers 250 mW for 50 mW of RF drive. Find PDC, the drain efficiency, the PAE and the heat dissipated.
   1. PDC = 3.3 × 0.300 = 0.990 W.
   2. ηD = 0.250/0.990 = 0.253 = 25.3 %.
   3. PAE = (0.250 − 0.050)/0.990 = 0.202 = 20.2 %.
   4. Heat = PDC + Pin − Pout = 0.990 + 0.050 − 0.250 = 0.790 W, more than three times the RF output.
   5. The PA gain is only 10 log₁₀(250/50) = 7.0 dB, which is why PAE is so far below ηD.
   Answer: PDC = 0.99 W, ηD = 25.3 %, PAE = 20.2 %, and 0.79 W becomes heat. */
