/* book Worked example 2: Q: Design the output of a 2 GHz Class A PA with VDD = 3.3 V, Vknee = 0.3 V and Imax = 1 A. Find Ropt, the output power in W and dBm, the DC power and the efficiency, and the L-section that matches a 50 Ω antenna to Ropt. What is the efficiency at 6 dB back-off?
   1. Ropt = 2(3.3 − 0.3)/1 = 6.0 Ω.
   2. Peak voltage swing 3.0 V, peak current swing 0.5 A: Pout = 3.0 × 0.5/2 = 0.75 W = 10 log₁₀ 750 = 28.8 dBm.
   3. IDC = 0.5 A, so PDC = 3.3 × 0.5 = 1.65 W and ηD = 0.75/1.65 = 45.5 % (below 50 % because of Vknee).
   4. L-section from 50 Ω down to 6 Ω: Q = √(50/6 − 1) = 2.708. Series reactance on the 6 Ω side Xs = Q × 6 = 16.25 Ω; shunt reactance on the 50 Ω side Xp = 50/Q = 18.46 Ω.
   5. At 2 GHz (ω = 1.257 × 10¹⁰ rad/s): series L = 16.25/ω = 1.29 nH; shunt C = 1/(ω × 18.46) = 4.31 pF. Check: (6 + j16.25) in parallel with −j18.46 gives 50.0 Ω.
   6. At 6 dB back-off a Class A stage still draws 1.65 W, so η = 45.5 % × 10−0.6 = 45.5 % × 0.251 = 11.4 %.
   Answer: Ropt = 6 Ω, Pout = 0.75 W (28.8 dBm), PDC = 1.65 W, ηD = 45.5 %; a 1.29 nH series inductor and a 4.31 pF shunt capacitor match 50 Ω to 6 Ω; η falls to 11.4 % at 6 dB back-off. */
